    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: 'The pack is divided roughly equally between players; each holds cards as a face-down pile. Going clockwise, each player places the top card of their pile face up in the centre. When a Jack is played, the first player to slap the pile wins the centre pile and adds it face down to the bottom of their pile; play continues from the left of the winner. Do not peek at your card before turning it; everyone must see it at once. False slap: if you slap when the top card is not a Jack, you give your top card to the player who played that card. If you run out of cards, you may still slap the next Jack to re-enter; if you fail or false-slap, you are out. The player who has all the cards wins.',
    Player: 'The pack is divided roughly equally between players; each holds cards as a face-down pile. Going clockwise, each player places the top card of their pile face up in the centre. When a Jack is played, the first player to slap the pile wins the centre pile and adds it face down to the bottom of their pile; play continues from the left of the winner. Do not peek at your card before turning it; everyone must see it at once. False slap: if you slap when the top card is not a Jack, you give your top card to the player who played that card. If you run out of cards, you may still slap the next Jack to re-enter; if you fail or false-slap, you are out. The player who has all the cards wins.',
    objective: 'Collect the entire deck by winning the center pile when a Jack is played. The first player to slap the center pile when a Jack appears wins the pile and adds it to the bottom of their face-down stack.',
    gameplay: 'The pack is divided roughly equally between players; each holds cards as a face-down pile. Going clockwise, each player places the top card of their pile face up in the centre. When a Jack is played, the first player to slap the pile wins the centre pile and adds it face down to the bottom of their pile; play continues from the left of the winner. Do not peek at your card before turning it; everyone must see it at once. False slap: if you slap when the top card is not a Jack, you give your top card to the player who played that card. If you run out of cards, you may still slap the next Jack to re-enter; if you fail or false-slap, you are out. The player who has all the cards wins.',
    keyRules: [
      'Turn your card so all players see it at once; do not peek in advance.',
      'Only Jacks are slapped; first to slap the pile wins it.',
      'False slap: give your top card to the player who played the wrongly-slapped card.',
      'Run out of cards: one more chance to slap a Jack to re-enter; otherwise you are out.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
