      'Setup example: 26 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Collect the entire deck by winning the center pile when a Jack is played. The first player to slap the center pile when a Jack appears wins the pile and adds it to the bottom of their face-down stack.',
      'Turn-flow example: The pack is divided roughly equally between players; each holds cards as a face-down pile. Going clockwise, each player places the top card of their pile face up in the centre. When a Jack is played, the first player to slap the pile wins the centre pile and adds it face down to the bottom of their pile; play continues from the left of the winner. Do not peek at your card before turning it; everyone must see it at once. False slap: if you slap when the top card is not a Jack, you give your top card to the player who played that card. If you run out of cards, you may still slap the next Jack to re-enter; if you fail or false-slap, you are out. The player who has all the cards wins.',
